Interpreting timing violations
If STA reports:
WNS ≥ 0 ns → timing is met.
WNS < 0 ns → there is a setup timing violation.
Hold violations appear when minimum-delay requirements are not satisfied.
Typical fixes for timing violations
Pipeline the design
Insert registers to shorten long combinational paths.
Reduce combinational logic depth
Split complex arithmetic or logic into multiple stages.
Increase the clock period
Relax timing constraints if higher frequency is unnecessary.
Re-synthesize with optimization
Use higher-effort optimization or timing-driven synthesis.
Cell sizing / buffering
Replace slow cells with faster drive-strength variants or insert buffers.
